## 2. The Authenticated Session Hand-off (Deep Authenticated Scanning)
Nuclei is incredibly fast, but it struggles to log into websites that use complex OAuth, CAPTCHAs, or multi-step JavaScript login forms. [14] 
You use Puppeteer to handle the complex login logic, extract the valid session cookie, and pass that authorization header directly to Nuclei so it can scan the protected dashboard area. [15, 16] 

* Step 1: Puppeteer logs in and gets the cookie (login.js)

import puppeteer from 'puppeteer';import fs from 'fs';
const browser = await puppeteer.launch({ executablePath: '/usr/bin/chromium-browser', args: ['--no-sandbox'] });const page = await browser.newPage();await page.goto('https://target.com');
// Automate typing and logging inawait page.type('#user', 'bounty-hunter');await page.type('#pass', 'SecretPass!');await page.click('#submit');await page.waitForNavigation();
// Grab the session cookiesconst cookies = await page.cookies();const session = cookies.find(c => c.name === 'SESSIONID')?.value;
// Write out a header string for Nuclei
fs.writeFileSync('headers.txt', `Authorization: Bearer ${session}`);await browser.close();

* Step 2: Run Nuclei using the cookie header generated by Puppeteer

node login.js
nuclei -u https://target.com -H "$(cat headers.txt)" -t vulnerabilities/

